;
; V8 calibration definition extension sample
;
; _________________________________________________________________________
; Each *.cax8 file name must begin with the same name as the EFILive supplied *.cam file for the target calibration.
;
; To lookup the name of the EFILive supplied *.cam file:
;   1. Load a tune file with the target calibration,
;   2. Open any EFILive defined calibration,
;   3. Select the [Provider] tab page and observe the file name and the folder name.
;
; For example, if the EFILive supplied *.cam file is: C:\Program Files (x86)\EFILive\V8\Cam\E38\12649046.cam
; then you must place your *.cax8 file(s) in the folder: \Documents\EFILive\V8\User Defined cax8\E38\
;
; In most cases the *.cax8 file name will be the same as the calibration's operating system number. However, some
; Allison transmission calibrations use the calibration ID instead of the operating system number. And some
; Cummins calibrations use a modified operating system number. So be careful to choose the correct file name for your *.cax8 file.
;
; You may create multiple *.cax8 files for the same calibration. Each *.cax8 file name must start with the matching sequence
; as described above but may have additional characters appended to the filename. For example:
;
; - 12649046.cax8
; - 12649046_Options.cax8
; - 12649046_Code1.cax8
; - 12649046_Testing.cax8
;
; All of those *.cax8 files will be loaded when a tune file is opened that uses the EFILive defined 12649046.cam.
;
; To ensure that all calibration names (and other identifiers) are unique across all *.cax8 files, you should define a
; "UniqueID" value in the [Provider] section below so that each *.cax8 file has a unique "UniqueID" value.
; Failing to provide a UniqueID will reuslt in the EFILive software assigning an automatically generated unqiue ID
; in the range U00..U99.
;
; After modifying and saving a *.cax8 file, you can force the EFILive V8 tune editor to re-load the modified cax8 file(s) by
; pressing the hotkey combination Ctrl+Alt+X while the editor is open.
;
; _________________________________________________________________________
; Comment character is the semicolon.
; All text on a single line following the first semicolon (outside of a quoted string) will be ignored.
;
; _________________________________________________________________________
; Line continuation character is the backslash \ character. Placing it at the end of a line indicates that the next
; line is a continuation of that line. The line continuation character will be ignored (as a continuation) if it
; appears within a quoted string.
;
; _________________________________________________________________________
; The $INCLUDE directive may be used to include the contents of another named file.
; For example, to include another file called Common Data.txt, do this:
; $Include Common Data.txt
; The filename consists of all text following the $Include directive to the end of the line.
; You may nest multiple include files.
;
; _________________________________________________________________________
; Numeric values can be specified in decimal or hexadecimal
;
; Decimal numbers are entered as normal/standard numbers, scientific notation is acceptable.
; Examples:
; 123
; 12.34
; -12.34
; 1.234E5 (is 1.234 x 10^5 = 123400)
; 1.234E-5 (is 1.234 x 10^-5 = 0.00001234)
;
; Hexadecimal numbers are entered with the prefix $
; Examples:
; $F0        ( = decimal 240)
; $4A3C      ( = decimal 19004)
; $800EEF    ( = decimal 8392431)
;
; _________________________________________________________________________
; All values and units in this cax8 file MUST be specified using metric units (or non-system-specific
; units such as step, count) and the units must valid units as defined in the V8 software under
; the Edit->Properties->General->Units tab page.
;
; When the calibration is displayed, the user can select the actual display units. So, for example if a
; calibration is defined using km/h, then when the calibration is displayed, the user will be presented
; with all other speed related units such as mph, feet/sec, meters/second etc. The user can choose to
; display the calibration in any of those preferred units, the V8 software will automatically convert
; the displayed values to the selected units.
;
; _________________________________________________________________________
; Lists are separated using the comma and/or space character. When multiple, comma or space separated items
; are listed, if any item contains a comma or space character, that item must be enclosed in double quotes.
;
; For example:
; A list of gear names without double quotes, like this: First Gear, Second Gear, Third Gear
; will be interpreted as six individual items: First, Gear, Second, Gear, Third and Gear.
;
; The same list of gear names with double quotes, like this: "First Gear","Second Gear","Third Gear"
; will be interpreted as three individual items: First Gear, Second Gear and Third Gear.
;
; _________________________________________________________________________
; Pre-defined default values are substituted if any value is specified as a dot.
;
; _________________________________________________________________________
; Calibration IDs (Cal ID) can be any text. Unlike V7, the Cal ID is not restricted to a letter followed by 4 digits.
;
; _________________________________________________________________________
;
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Provider contains information about the definitions and the person or company that provided them.
;
[Provider]
;-------------------------------------------------- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;Key                                                Value
;-------------------------------------------------- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Version                                             8.3.1.0                ; major.minor.release.version - it is recommended to keep the major.minor.release values in-synch with the EFILive V8 software.
Date                                                2020.08.01             ; year.month.day
Name                                                Provider Name          ; Provider Name, Name of the person or company that created this file.
UniqueID                                            ID                     ; Unique ID to prefix all names in this file to ensure uniqueness across different cax8 files.
HelpFile                                            Filename               ; Name of the file that contains extra information about this file - not currently supported.
Description                                         Description            ; Brief description of the contents of this file.
Url                                                 http://www.website.com ; URL of the person or company that created this file.
Contact                                             name@company.com       ; Email contact of the person or company that created this file.

;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Definitions allow common or complex values to be defined as simple text
; To dereference a definition name in a calibration definition, enclose the name in curly braces.
;
[Define]
;-------------------------------------------------- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;Definition                                         Value
;-------------------------------------------------- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Name                                                Substitution

;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Address offsets allow you to use the address definitions from a similar calibration that only differs by
; a few blocks of calibration data that are offset by some number of bytes.
; This feature is most useful if you define the addresses for each calibration in the [Define] section via an included/common file,
; then reference those defined addresses in the [Data] section of multiple different cax8 files.
;
[AddressOffset]
;-------------- --------------- -------------------
;Start Address  End Address     Offset
;-------------- --------------- -------------------
Address1        Address2        +/- offset
Address3        Address4        +/- offset
etc.

;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Enums (enumerations) are used to display text values in place of numeric values.
;
[Enum]
;-------------------------------------------------- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;Enumeration                                        Tag/Value List
;-------------------------------------------------- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Name                                                "1=Red,2=Green,3=Blue"

;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Axis define the labels that are displayed across the top and/or down the left side of calibration tables.
;
[Axis]
;-------------------------------------------------- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;Axis Name                                          Axis Labels
;-------------------------------------------------- ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
rpm0to6000x13                                       "0,500,1000,1500,2000,2500,3000,3500,4000,4500,5000,5500,6000

;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The Data section contains each calibration's data definition.
; It defines the way the calibration is retrieved/stored in the controller's memory.
;
[Data]
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------- -------- -------- -------- ---------------- ---------------- ---- -------- ---- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ----------------
;                                                                                          X        Y                                                                                                                                 X                Y
;Cal ID                                                                           Address  ColCount RowCount Factor           Offset           Inv  Size     Type DataOffset       HardMin          HardMax          DataUnits        ColUnits         RowUnits         Deposit          Endian           Align
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------- -------- -------- -------- ---------------- ---------------- ---- -------- ---- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ----------------
; Cal ID         The unique name of the calibration. Do not re-use existing EFILive calibration IDs.
;                Calibration names are case sensitive so the name "A1234" is considered to be different than "a1234"
;
; Address        Contains the address of the calibration. If a calibration consists of two or more
;                  non-contiguous columns, then a list of addresses may be specified where each
;                  address is the address of the first cell in each column.
;
; ColCount       The number of columns in the calibration. Default = 1.
; RowCount       The number of rows in the calibration. Default = 1.
;
; Factor         The factor by which to multiply the raw controller values to convert them into the appropriate metric units. Default = 1.
; Offset         The offset to add to the raw controller values to convert them into the appropriate metric units. Default = 0.
; Inv            If set to 1, then invert the raw value prior to applying factor and offset. A raw value of zero
;                  cannot be computed and will be displayed as an empty cell. Default = 0.
;
; Size           The size in bits of each cell in the calibration. Required.
;                  The size can be any of the following three formats:
;                  - B     where B is the number of bits - in this case, M defaults to all bits and S defaults to 0.
;                  - B:M   where M is the bit mask - in this case S defaults to 0. Only data bits matching the 1 bits in (B<<S) will be read/written from/to the bin image.
;                  - B:M:S where S is the bit-shift, bits will be shifted S bits right when reading and S bits left when writing.
;
;                  A value is extracted from the bin file as follows:
;                  1. Extract as many whole bytes starting at the calibration's address as is required to satisfy the bit count.
;                  2. Shift the mask left by shift bits.
;                  3. Copy all bits from the extracted bytes that match the 1-bits in the mask.
;                  4. Shift the copied bits right by shift bits.
;
;                  For example: assume Size = 16:$00FF:4 bits=16, Mask=$00FF, shift=4 (i.e. we are interested in these 8 bits from the middle of the 16 bits: ....11111111....)
;                               and Bin data = $56,$78
;                  1. Extract 16 bits (2 bytes of data) = $5678
;                  2. Shift Mask left by 4 bits, effective mask = $0FF0
;                  3. $5678 AND $0FF0 = $0670
;                  4. Shift right by 4 bits, value = $0067 - we've successfully extracted the $67 from the middle of $5678
;
; Type           The data type of the calibration. Required.
;                  Must be one of:
;                  - UNM values are stored as unsigned numeric.
;                  - SNM values are stored as signed numeric (two's compliment).
;                  - SED values are stored as state encoded data (or enumerated types).
;                  - FLT values are stored as 4 byte IEEE floating point values.
;
; DataOffset     The number of bytes from the calibration address to the first cell of data. Default = 0.
;
; HardMin        The minimum value that can be set for this calibration. Default = computed based on data type, and bit count.
; HardMax        The maximum value that can be set for this calibration. Default = computed based on data type, and bit count.
;
; DataUnits      The metric units that will be used to display the calibration. Required.
;                    The units MUST be defined in: Edit->Properties->General->Units.
;                    The units MUST not be defined as "US" - US Customary units may instead be selected by the user when the calibration is displayed.
; ColUnits       The metric units that will be used to display the top labels. Required.
;                    The units MUST be defined in: Edit->Properties->General->Units.
;                    The units MUST not be defined as "US" - US Customary units may instead be selected by the user when the calibration is displayed.
; RowUnits       The metric units that will be used to display the left labels. Required.
;                    The units MUST be defined in: Edit->Properties->General->Units.
;                    The units MUST not be defined as "US" - US Customary units may instead be selected by the user when the calibration is displayed.
;
; Deposit        The order in which a table is stored in memory. Default = controller's default.
;                  Must be one of:
;                  - Col = data is stored as a sequence of columns.
;                  - Row = data is stored as a sequence of rows.
;
; Endian         The endian-ness of the calibration's values. Default = controller's default.
;                  Must be one of
;                  - Intel = numerical values are stored least significant byte first.
;                  - Motorola = numerical values are stored most significant byte first.
;
; Align          The byte alignment of the first cell of each column (if Deposit=Col) or
;                of each row (if Deposit=Row). Default = controller's default.
;                  Must be one of:
;                  - Byte = aligned to an 8 bit boundary.
;                  - Word = aligned to a 16 bit boundary.
;                  - DWord = aligned to a 32 bit boundary.
;                  - QWord = aligned to a 64 bit boundary.
;
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The Calibration section contains each calibration's display definition,
; it defines the way the calibration is displayed in the EFILive software.
;
[Calibration]
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------- --- -------------------------------- --------- -------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------- ----- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ----------------
;Cal_ID                                                                           Seg Tree                             Flags     Display  SoftMin          SoftMax          Enum             Options          DataFmt    DPrec ColFmt           ColDesc          ColLabels        RowFmt           RowDesc          RowLabels
;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------- --- -------------------------------- --------- -------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------- ----- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ---------------- ----------------
; Cal ID         The unique name of the calibration which matches the equivalent name in the [Data] section. Do not re-use existing EFILive calibration IDs.
;
; Seg            Determines the top-level branch in which this calibration will be displayed. Required.
;                Segment numbers vary between controller types. Refer to the file: \Program Files (x86)\EFILive\V8\V7toV8_Segments.ini for a list of
;                segment numbers and descriptions for each contorller type that is supported by the V8 tune editor.
;
; Tree           The backslash separated list of tree branches under which this calibration will be displayed.
;                  For example: "Spark\General"
;
; Flags          Bitmapped flags that provide extra information to the EFILive software about this calibration.
;                  $00000007 = Calibration is available (for scripting) but not visible to the end user for editing.
;                  $00000010 = Calibration is not editable - effectively read-only.
;                  $00000020 = Calibration is not available in US installations (for EPA compliance).
;                  $00000040 = Calibration is not saved back into the bin image, even if it has been modified.
;                  $00000080 = Calibration is only for information or display somewhere other than the editor's tree view.
;                  $00001000 = Display calibration as raw hex values.
;                  $00004000 = Display without value weighting or cell color (i.e. for parameter lists).
;                  $00010000 = Do not display any 2D or 3D graphic image (i.e. for parameter lists and DTCs).
;                  $00020000 = Display multi column tables as 2D line-chart instead of 3D surface.
;                  $10000000 = Calibration is an editable axis.
;                  $100350F7 = Only allowed bits in flags
;                  All other bits are reserved/ignored and should be set to 0 for future compatibility.
;
; Display        Calibration's display format. Default = Value.
;                  Must be one of:
;                  - Value =      a single cell value.
;                  - Curve =      a column of cells.
;                  - Map =        a table of cells.
;                  - List =       a repeating list of single values.
;                  - DtcStatic =  a list of diagnostic trouble codes defined in the cax8 file.
;                  - DtcDynamic = a list of diagnostic trouble codes defined in the tune file.
;
;                For the two DTC styles, the descriptions for the DTCs are loaded from the *.dtc files in the folder: \Program Files (x86)\EFILive\V8\Config\*.dtc
;                If you want to add/modify the DTC descriptions, create your own DTC files in the \Documents\EFILive\V8\Config\DTC folder with the same names
;                as the EFILive supplied *.dtc files but with *.txt extensions instead. Place each DTC Description pair on a separate line in the text file(s).
;                The files are named using the following convention: "mfg_type.txt" where:
;                  mfg is one of:
;                    gm: General Motors
;                    ch: Cummins light duty
;                    hd: Cummins heavy duty - this file has no _type suffix.
;                  type is one of:
;                    p: Engine codes (beginning with "P")
;                    b: Body codes (beginning with "B")
;                    c: Chassis codes (beginning with "C")
;                    u: Network codes (beginning with "U")
;                The DTC descriptions are only loaded once (the first time they are displayed).
;                If you modify any of the DTC description text files, you must re-start the EFILive V8 software to cause the modified descriptions to be re-loaded.
;
; SoftMin        The recommended/sane minimum limit that can be set for this calibration. Default = HardMin.
; SoftMax        The recommended/sane maximum limit that can be set for this calibration. Default = HardMax.
;
; Enum           The name of the enumeration defined in the [Enum] section that will be used to convert the calibration's
;                  numeric values into text values.
;
; Options        Not used, set to a single dot.
;
; DataFmt        The format string for the calibration's title. Default = "<d> <u>".
;                  Substitutions:
;                    <d> replace with the description.
;                    <u> replace with the currently selected display units.
;                    <U> replace with the currently selected display units' description.
;
; DPrec          Number of decimal points used to display the calibration value(s). Default = 0.
;
; ColFmt         The format string for the top axis title, see DataFmt for substitutions. Default = No title.
; ColDesc        The description for the top axis. Default = No description.
; ColLabels      The name of an axis defined in the [Axis] section. Default = No Labels.
;                  Prefix:
;                  - ' (single quote) for a string literal.
;                  - @xxx to reference calibration "xxx" that defines the axis labels
;
; RowFmt         The format string for the left axis title, see DataFmt for substitutions. Default = No title.
; RowDesc        The description for the left axis. Default = No description.
; RowLabels      The name of an axis defined in the [Axis] section. Default = No Labels.
;                  Prefix:
;                  - ' (single quote) for a string literal.
;                  - @xxx to reference calibration "xxx" that defines the axis labels

;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Descriptions for each calibration
;
[Description]
;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
; Descriptions are constructed using simple HTML.
; Each calibration's description must begin with an HTML comment in
; the following format:
; <!-- #xxxxxxxx dddddddd -->
;   where
;     xxxxxxxx is the calibration's name
;     dddddddd is the calibration's description
;
; All text following that comment, until the next such comment becomes
; the calibration's description.
;
; - Use <br> to specify a new line, i.e. a new paragraph.
; - Enclose calibration names in curly braces to create links to those calibrations.
; - Add a hyphen prefix to the name to create a bullet-point list item.

